'''Aavas Financiers,''' also known as '''Aavas''', is a [[Jaipur]] based housing [[finance]] company known for providing [[home loans]] in the rural and semi-urban locations of [[India]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Aavas Financiers to raise ₹100 crore through NCDs|url=https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/money-and-banking/aavas-financiers-to-raise-100-crore-through-ncds/article33417353.ece|url-status=live|access-date=2021-03-19|website=@businessline|date=25 December 2020 |language=en|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201225102557/https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/money-and-banking/aavas-financiers-to-raise-100-crore-through-ncds/article33417353.ece |archive-date=2020-12-25 }}</ref><ref>{{Cite book|last=Baid|first=Gautam|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=84W-DwAAQBAJ&dq=Aavas+Financiers&pg=PT512|title=The Joys of Compounding: The Passionate Pursuit of Lifelong Learning, Revised and Updated|date=2021-03-19|publisher=Columbia University Press|isbn=978-0-231-55211-0|language=en}}</ref> Aavas is registered with [[National Housing Bank]] as a Housing Finance Company and was granted the license in August 2011.<ref>{{Cite web|title=AAVAS.IN {{!}} Aavas Financiers Ltd. Company Profile & Executives - WSJ|url=https://www.wsj.com/market-data/quotes/IN/XNSE/AAVAS/company-people|access-date=2021-03-19|website=www.wsj.com}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Aavas Financiers Ltd - Company Profile and News|url=https://www.bloomberg.com/profile/company/1378530D:IN|access-date=2021-03-19|website=Bloomberg.com|language=en}}</ref>

== History ==

Aavas was incorporated in February 2011. It formally started its operations in March 2012.<ref>{{Cite web|date=2017-05-09|title=IFC to invest $40 mn in Aavas Financiers {{!}} M&A Critique|url=https://mnacritique.mergersindia.com/news/ifc-to-invest-40-mn-in-aavas-financiers/|access-date=2021-03-19|language=en-US}}</ref> 

The company issued its [[Initial public offering|IPO]] in October 2018.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Aavas Financiers Raises Rs 520 Cr From 34 Anchor Investors, IPO Opens On September 25|url=https://www.moneycontrol.com/news/business/markets/aavas-financiers-raises-rs-520-cr-from-34-anchor-investors-ipo-opens-on-september-25-2982601.html|url-status=live|access-date=2021-03-19|website=Moneycontrol|date=24 September 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180924190506/https://www.moneycontrol.com/news/business/markets/aavas-financiers-raises-rs-520-cr-from-34-anchor-investors-ipo-opens-on-september-25-2982601.html |archive-date=2018-09-24 }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Aavas Financiers IPO Review - Aavas Financiers IPO Dates, Issue Price, Subscription and Allotment Status - The Economic Times|url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/aavas-financiers-ltd/ipos/companyid-35834.cms|url-status=live|access-date=2021-03-19|website=economictimes.indiatimes.com|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200529181302/https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/aavas-financiers-ltd/ipos/companyid-35834.cms |archive-date=2020-05-29 }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Aavas Financiers' IPO: Here's All You Need To Know|url=https://www.bloombergquint.com/ipos/aavas-financiers-ipo-heres-all-you-need-to-know|access-date=2021-03-19|website=BloombergQuint|date=24 September 2018 |language=en}}</ref> Shortly after the IPO, [[CDC Group]] invested {{INR}}200 crore in Aavas.<ref>{{Cite news|agency=Press Trust of India|date=2018-12-20|title=Aavas raises Rs 200 cr from UK's CDC group|work=Business Standard India|url=https://www.business-standard.com/article/pti-stories/aavas-raises-rs-200-cr-from-uk-s-cdc-group-118122001019_1.html|access-date=2021-03-19}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=www.ETRealty.com|title=Aavas Financiers raises Rs 200 crore from UK's CDC Group - ET RealEstate|url=https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/allied-industries/aavas-financiers-raises-rs-200-crore-from-uks-cdc-group/67186697|access-date=2021-03-19|website=ETRealty.com|language=en}}</ref>

In September 2019, the company received {{INR}}345 crore investment from [[International Finance Corporation]], a member of the [[World Bank Group]].<ref>{{Cite news|last=ANI|date=2019-09-17|title=Aavas Financiers raises Rs 345 crore from IFC through NCDs|work=Business Standard India|url=https://www.business-standard.com/article/news-ani/aavas-financiers-raises-rs-345-crore-from-ifc-through-ncds-119091700345_1.html|access-date=2021-03-19}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Affordable housing financier Aavas gets Rs 345 cr funding from IFC|url=https://www.outlookindia.com/newsscroll/affordable-housing-financier-aavas-gets-rs-345-cr-funding-from-ifc/1620209|access-date=2021-03-19|website=Outlook India}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=www.ETRealty.com|title=IFC invests Rs 345 crore in Aavas Financiers - ET RealEstate|url=https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/allied-industries/ifc-invests-rs-345-crore-in-aavas-financiers/71159825|access-date=2021-03-19|website=ETRealty.com|language=en}}</ref> In March 2020, Aavas signed an agreement with [[Asian Development Bank]] for receiving loan amount of $60 million specially targeting towards the 'women in lower income group'.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Affordable housing firm Aavas gets $60m ADB loan|url=https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/news/real-estate/affordable-housing-firm-aavas-gets-60m-adb-loan/article31216995.ece|url-status=live|access-date=2021-03-19|website=@businessline|date=31 March 2020 |language=en|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200402091117/https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/news/real-estate/affordable-housing-firm-aavas-gets-60m-adb-loan/article31216995.ece |archive-date=2020-04-02 }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|last=Market|first=Capital|date=2020-03-30|title=Aavas Financiers gains on securing ADB loan to boost housing finance in India|work=Business Standard India|url=https://www.business-standard.com/article/news-cm/aavas-financiers-gains-on-securing-adb-loan-to-boost-housing-finance-in-india-120033001134_1.html|access-date=2021-03-19}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=2021-03-19|title=Kedaara-backed Aavas Financiers to raise loan from Asian Development Bank|url=https://www.vccircle.com/kedaara-backed-aavas-financiers-to-raise-loan-from-asian-development-bank|url-status=live|access-date=2021-02-18|website=VCCircle|language=en-US|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201127080636/https://www.vccircle.com/kedaara-backed-aavas-financiers-to-raise-loan-from-asian-development-bank |archive-date=2020-11-27 }}</ref> In December 2020, to promote the concept of Green Housing, [[International Finance Corporation]] signed an agreement with the company.<ref>{{Cite web|last=www.ETEnergyworld.com|title=IFC, Aavas Financiers sign pact for affordable green housing finance for low-income borrowers - ET EnergyWorld|url=https://energy.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/renewable/ifc-aavas-financiers-sign-pact-for-affordable-green-housing-finance-for-low-income-borrowers/79604732|url-status=live|access-date=2021-03-19|website=ETEnergyworld.com|language=en|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201207120052/https://energy.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/renewable/ifc-aavas-financiers-sign-pact-for-affordable-green-housing-finance-for-low-income-borrowers/79604732 |archive-date=2020-12-07 }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=2021-03-19|title=New project to help catalyse affordable green housing finance in India|url=https://www.energylivenews.com/2020/12/04/new-project-to-help-catalyse-affordable-green-housing-finance-in-india/|url-status=live|access-date=2021-02-18|website=Energy Live News|language=en-US|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201204153938/https://www.energylivenews.com/2020/12/04/new-project-to-help-catalyse-affordable-green-housing-finance-in-india/ |archive-date=2020-12-04 }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=admin|date=2021-03-19|title=IFC signs agreement for affordable green housing in India|url=https://greentechlead.com/green-building/ifc-signs-agreement-for-affordable-green-housing-in-india-36727|url-status=live|access-date=2021-02-18|website=GreentechLead|language=en-US|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201203055408/https://greentechlead.com/green-building/ifc-signs-agreement-for-affordable-green-housing-in-india-36727 |archive-date=2020-12-03 }}</ref><ref>{{Cite book|last=Sharma|first=Sandeep Ravidutt|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=ZC8PEAAAQBAJ&dq=Aavas+Financiers&pg=PR7|title=ProjectX India: 15th December 2020 {{!}} Tracking Multisector Projects from India|date=2021-03-19|publisher=Sandeep Ravidutt Sharma|language=en}}</ref>

== Operations ==
As of March 31, 2026, Aavas has 435 branches operating in 15 states and UT of India.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Statement of audited financial results for the quarter and year ended March 31, 2026 published in Financial Express Epaper 06 May 2026 |url=https://epaper.financialexpress.com/4148683/Mumbai/May-06-2026#page/3/1}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|date=2026-05-06|title=Aavas Financiers Limited: [ICRA]AA-(Stable) rating assigned|url=https://www.icra.in/Rationale/ShowRationaleReport/?Id=99007}}</ref> Presently the company is headed by Manu Singh as CEO.<ref>{{Cite web|date=2023-05-03|title=MarketWatch Aavas Financiers Profile|url=https://www.financialexpress.com/business/industry-aavas-financiers-board-appoints-manu-singh-as-md-ceo-4213196/|access-date=2026-04-20|website=www.financialexpress.com|language=en}}</ref>

The equity shares of Aavas are listed on [[Bombay Stock Exchange]] where it is a constituent of the BSE 150 Midcap, and the [[National Stock Exchange of India]] where it is a constituent of Nifty Midcap 150.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Aavas Financiers Listing Information - The Economic Times|url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/aavas-financiers-ltd/infocompanylisting/companyid-35834.cms|access-date=2021-03-19|website=economictimes.indiatimes.com}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Stock Share Price {{!}} Get Quote {{!}} BSE|url=https://www.bseindia.com/stock-share-price/aavas-financiers-ltd/aavas/541988/|access-date=2021-03-19|website=www.bseindia.com}}</ref>

